# Design rules - Indoor Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor
# Stackup: JLC04161H-7628 equivalent, 4 layer, 1.6 mm
#   F.Cu  0.035 | prepreg 7628 0.2104 er=4.4 | In1.Cu (GND) | core 1.065
#   | In2.Cu (PWR/SHLD) | prepreg 7628 0.2104 | B.Cu 0.035
# See LAYOUT.md for the reasoning behind every number here.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: for a given constraint type the LAST matching rule wins. The
# exemptions at the bottom of this file have to stay below the broad fabrication
# minimums, or the minimums override them and the exemption silently does
# nothing. Verified by injecting geometry that should and should not trip.

(version 1)

# Fabrication floor. This has to sit ABOVE every specific width rule: last
# matching rule wins, and this one matches every track, so leaving it at the
# bottom silently overrode all of them. Caught by injecting a 0.3 mm track on
# /GND_PVSS2 and getting no violation.
(rule "Fab minimum track"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.127mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'Track'"))

# Clearance floor, hoisted for the same reason as the track floor above: it
# matches every pair, so every stricter rule below this line must come after it.
(rule "Fab minimum clearance"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.127mm)))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RF path --
# 50 ohm microstrip on F.Cu referenced to the In1.Cu ground plane.
# W = 0.36 mm. This is JLCPCB's own impedance calculator output - 14.12 mil for
# 50 ohm single-ended on L1 over L2 in JLC04161H-7628 - not a hand calculation.
(rule "RF 50R trace width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.34mm) (opt 0.36mm) (max 0.42mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'RF'"))

# The RF path must not be crowded. Anything closer than 0.5 mm couples into it
# or perturbs the impedance.
(rule "RF clearance to other nets"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'RF' && B.NetClass != 'RF'"))

# A via in the RF path adds inductance and a stub, and breaks the reference.
# The whole ANT -> matching -> antenna run belongs on F.Cu.
(rule "No vias in the RF path"
	(constraint disallow via)
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'RF'"))

# Nordic's two RF grounding rules, which are invisible in a netlist and so are
# split into their own nets and rejoined by net ties NT1 and NT2. See
# HARDWARE.md section 2 and LAYOUT.md section 2.
#
# 1. C6 grounds ONLY at pin 32 (VSS_PA) on the top layer, and pin 32 reaches the
#    centre pad only underneath the package. A via anywhere on GND_PA defeats
#    that, so no vias, and nothing on any layer but F.Cu.
(rule "C6 ground takes no vias"
	(constraint disallow via)
	(condition "A.NetName == '/GND_PA'"))

(rule "C6 ground stays on the top layer"
	(constraint disallow track)
	(condition "A.NetName == '/GND_PA' && !A.existsOnLayer('F.Cu')"))

# 2. C9 grounds only on the bottom ground layer. A short stub from its pad to a
#    via is unavoidable; touching an inner plane is not.
(rule "C9 ground never touches an inner plane"
	(constraint disallow track)
	(condition "A.NetName == '/GND_C9' && (A.existsOnLayer('In1.Cu') || A.existsOnLayer('In2.Cu'))"))

# The remaining half of each rule is placement, not routing, and is asserted in
# tools_gen_pcb.py instead: NT1 goes under the U1 centre pad on F.Cu, NT2 goes
# on B.Cu, NT3 goes at the PVSS2 via beside U2 pin 6.

# ------------------------------------------------- capacitive front end ----
# The switching nodes are the main aggressors: nPM1300 SW2 at 3.6 MHz in PWM
# and the nRF54L15 DCC node. Keep them well away from anything the FDC1004
# measures.
(rule "Sense away from switching nodes"
	(constraint clearance (min 3mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SENSE' && B.NetClass == 'SWITCH'"))

(rule "Shield away from switching nodes"
	(constraint clearance (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SHIELD' && B.NetClass == 'SWITCH'"))

(rule "Sense away from RF"
	(constraint clearance (min 2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SENSE' && B.NetClass == 'RF'"))

# Ground adjacent to a sense net is measured capacitance. It burns CAPDAC
# range and couples noise. The guard pour, not ground, is what surrounds sense.
(rule "Sense away from ground"
	(constraint clearance (min 1mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SENSE' && B.NetClass == 'Power'"))

# Guard is meant to hug the sense trace - tight coupling is the point.
(rule "Sense to shield spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.2mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SENSE' && B.NetClass == 'SHIELD'"))

# -------------------------------------------------------------- power ------
(rule "Power track width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'Power'"))

# 500 mA charge path plus system load. 0.8 mm on 1 oz outer copper is roughly
# a 10 C rise at 1 A - comfortable margin.
(rule "Charge path width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.8mm))
	# A.Net is NOT a valid property - it parses but evaluates false forever, so
	# this rule was dead. Every other rule in this file uses A.NetName. Caught by
	# injecting a 0.5 mm VBAT track: 0 violations with A.Net, 2 with A.NetName.
	#
	# These three lost their leading slash when they became power SYMBOLS rather
	# than text labels: a local label on the root sheet is "/VBAT", a global
	# power symbol is "VBAT". The rule matched neither for a while, which is the
	# same silent-dead-rule failure the comment above describes. Nets that are
	# still local labels - GND_PVSS2, GND_PA, GND_C9 - keep the slash.
	(condition "A.NetName == 'VBAT' || A.NetName == 'VBUS_IN' || A.NetName == 'VSYS'"))

# The buck switching node should be short and fat, never long and thin.
(rule "Switch node width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'SWITCH'"))

# nPM1300 PVSS2 is the BUCK2 POWER ground, not a general ground pin. Nordic's
# reference schematic annotates it "Net tie" and "Via to GND-layer": it reaches
# the plane at one controlled point rather than merging into the top-layer pour.
# It carries the SW2 return, so it gets the switch node's width. Must sit below
# "Power track width" - GND_PVSS2 is in the Power class and the later rule wins.
(rule "BUCK2 power ground is short and fat"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetName == '/GND_PVSS2'"))

# ------------------------------------------------------------ keepouts -----
# The antenna keepout is GONE. The PCB inverted-F was replaced by a U.FL
# receptacle (J5) feeding an external adhesive antenna, so Zone A is now ordinary
# board: ZoneB_GND floods it and there is nothing left to keep copper away from.
# The AntennaKeepout and AntennaCrossing rule areas were deleted with it.

# Sensirion SHT4x datasheet 5.3: soldering the central die pad or placing an
# exposed copper pad beneath it heat-sinks the internal heater and it stops
# meeting spec. No copper under the sensor except the four pin pads.
(rule "No copper under SHT45"
	(constraint disallow track via zone)
	(condition "A.insideArea('NoCopperSHT45')"))

# ------------------------------------------------------------ fabrication --
# JLCPCB 4 layer standard process floor. Tighten only if you pay for it.
#
# "Fab minimum clearance" is deliberately NOT here. It matches every pair of
# items, so sitting at the bottom it silently overrode every specific clearance
# rule in this file - the RF 0.5 mm rule, all four sense/shield rules. Exactly
# the trap that had already been found and fixed in the track_width family; the
# clearance family still had it. It now sits above the specific rules, next to
# "Fab minimum track". Caught by injecting a 0.38 mm /ANT track off U1 pin 31
# and getting 'Fab minimum clearance 0.127' instead of 'RF clearance 0.5'.
(rule "Fab minimum annular ring"
	(constraint annular_width (min 0.13mm)))

(rule "Fab minimum drill"
	(constraint hole_size (min 0.2mm)))

# Copper to board edge. 0.3 mm keeps the router away from live copper.
(rule "Edge clearance"
	(constraint edge_clearance (min 0.3mm)))

# Once the clearance floor stopped masking them, the RF and sense rules turned
# out to be unsatisfiable against fixed package geometry - a part's own two
# terminals are the vendor land pattern, not a routing decision.
#
#   C6 / C9 / C11   0201 shunt caps, 0.18 mm between their own pads
#   U1 pin 31       0.4 mm QFN pitch: 0.1968 mm to pins 30 and 32,
#                   0.1905 mm across the annulus to the centre pad
#
# Scoped to pad-to-pad inside one footprint, and named part by part so a custom
# footprint elsewhere on this board stays policed. Routing is unaffected: an RF
# *track* near any other net still gets the full 0.5 mm.
#
# NOTE: a condition string must be on ONE line. A multi-line condition does not
# just fail that rule - KiCad discards the whole .kicad_dru and silently falls
# back to netclass clearances only. Caught because every violation in the report
# was attributed to "netclass 'Power'" and not one custom rule name appeared.
(rule "RF pad pairs inside one footprint are package geometry"
	(constraint clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad' && ((A.memberOfFootprint('C6') && B.memberOfFootprint('C6')) || (A.memberOfFootprint('C9') && B.memberOfFootprint('C9')) || (A.memberOfFootprint('C11') && B.memberOfFootprint('C11')) || (A.memberOfFootprint('U1') && B.memberOfFootprint('U1')))"))

# FDC1004 is MSOP-10 on 0.5 mm pitch and TI put SHLD1 (pin 1) directly beside
# CIN1 (pin 2) - 0.15 mm of pad-to-pad against the 0.2 mm sense-to-shield rule.
# Nothing to route differently; the pinout is the pinout.
# The 0.5 mm rule exists to keep UNRELATED copper away from the RF path. Inside
# the matching network itself it is unsatisfiable and wrong: a 0201 shunt cap has
# 0.64 mm between its own hot and ground pads, so any trace leaving the hot pad is
# within 0.5 mm of the ground pad it returns through. Those grounds are part of
# the RF structure, not foreign copper. Inside the cluster, spacing is set by the
# 0201 land pattern and the fab floor.
#
# Scoped to the six matching-network footprints by name, so RF copper anywhere
# else on the board still gets the full 0.5 mm.
(rule "Matching network internal spacing is the 0201 land pattern"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('MatchingNetwork')"))

# A 0.38 mm trace cannot leave a 0.4 mm-pitch QFN pad row: it would sit 0.108 mm
# from pins 30 and 32, under even the 0.127 mm fab floor. The same is true of the
# GND_PA return landing on pad 32, which is 0.1968 mm from pin 31 by pitch alone.
# So inside a small window over the pin 30/31/32 escape, both width and clearance
# are governed by the package, not by the RF rules: the /ANT trace leaves at pad
# width (0.2032 mm) and flares to 0.38 mm once clear of the row.
#
# The neck is ~0.73 mm against lambda = 69 mm in FR4 - lambda/95, a lumped
# discontinuity, which is what Nordic's own reference layout does.
#
# 0.15 mm still sits above the 0.127 mm fab floor. The window is 1.30 x 1.25 mm
# and is drawn on the board as the QFNEscape rule area, so the rest of the RF run
# keeps the full 0.34-0.42 mm width and 0.5 mm clearance. Verified by injecting a
# violation just outside the window and confirming the full rules still fire.
(rule "QFN escape: track width is set by the 0.4 mm pad pitch"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('QFNEscape')"))

(rule "QFN escape: clearance is set by the 0.4 mm pad pitch"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('QFNEscape')"))

# The same argument as the QFN escape above, generalised from the pin 30/31/32
# window to every fine-pitch land pattern that something actually has to escape
# from. A track leaving one of these pads cannot be as wide as its net class
# asks for and cannot hold that class's clearance to the pad next door, because
# the neighbour spacing is the vendor land pattern:
#
#   U1  QFN48 0.4 mm pitch, 0.203 mm pads -> 0.2985 mm pad centre to neighbour
#   U2  QFN32 0.5 mm pitch, 0.254 mm pads -> 0.373 mm
#   U3  MSOP-10 0.5 mm pitch              -> 0.15 mm between adjacent pads
#   U5  HVSSOP-8 0.65 mm pitch            -> 0.15 mm between adjacent pads
#   J1  USB-C                             -> 0.25 mm, VBUS pad to the SBU beside it
#
# Worked example, and why nothing narrower is available: U1 pin 47 is /+3V3
# (Power, 0.25 mm) and sits next to pin 46 /DCC (SWITCH, 0.3 mm). Escaping west
# at width w leaves 0.298 - w/2 to pin 46, so satisfying 0.3 mm needs w < 0,
# and satisfying it is not possible at any width. The pins are 0.4 mm apart
# because the package says so.
#
# Drawn as the FinePitchFanout rule areas in tools_add_zones.py, which
# deliberately EXCLUDE U1's bottom pad row - that is where the RF escape lives,
# it already has its own QFNEscape window, and /ANT must keep the full 0.5 mm
# clearance and 0.34 mm minimum width. Everything else on that row escapes at
# 0.19 mm, which holds 0.2035 mm to its neighbours and needs no exemption.
(rule "Fine-pitch fanout: track width is set by the pad pitch"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('FinePitchFanout')"))

# The Type guards are load-bearing, and leaving them off is a trap worth
# naming: insideArea() is true for a ZONE whenever the zone OVERLAPS the area,
# not only where the two actually intersect. ZoneB_GND_F spans the whole
# electronics band and therefore crosses six of the seven FinePitchFanout
# windows, so without the guards this rule matched the ground pour against
# every track and via ON THE BOARD and dropped the pour's clearance to 0.15 mm
# everywhere. It showed up as 97 clearance violations attributed to this rule
# at coordinates nowhere near a QFN. The pour keeps its full 0.25 mm; only
# tracks and vias get the package-geometry exemption.
(rule "Fine-pitch fanout: clearance is set by the pad pitch"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('FinePitchFanout') && A.Type != 'Zone' && B.Type != 'Zone'"))

(rule "FDC1004 adjacent pins are package geometry"
	(constraint clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad' && A.memberOfFootprint('U3') && B.memberOfFootprint('U3')"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS MUST STAY LAST IN THE FILE. Last matching rule wins, and the QFN escape
# clearance rule above sets 0.15 mm for everything inside the QFNEscape area -
# which includes NT1's own pads, turning the net tie's whole reason for existing
# into a violation.
# NT1 has to bridge the pin-32 land to the centre pad, and the annulus between
# them is 0.1905 mm. Two pads plus 0.127 mm of clearance on each side needs
# 0.254 mm, so the tie cannot satisfy the fab minimum against U1's own pads.
# That is not a defect: on a board without the net split this would simply be
# one net and one piece of copper. Scoped to NT1 against U1 and nothing else.
(rule "VSS_PA net tie bridges the QFN annulus"
	(constraint clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('NT1') && B.memberOfFootprint('U1')"))
